                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="16330422" author="ptupitsyn" created="Thu, 18 Jan 2018 12:09:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Making dummy cache &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;replicated&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt; (same as SQL cache) solves the problem.&lt;br/&gt;
But dummy cache does not participate in the query at all, looks like a bug.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16330439" author="ptupitsyn" created="Thu, 18 Jan 2018 12:27:20 +0000"  >&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;.NET &lt;tt&gt;TestRemoteNodes&lt;/tt&gt; runs the example twice, and it fails only on the second run.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Java &lt;tt&gt;SqlDdlExample&lt;/tt&gt; is exactly the same, but the issue does not occur there (even if we run it multiple times with the same standalone nodes).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Adding sleep(3000) before the problematic query fixes the issue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="16330469" author="ptupitsyn" created="Thu, 18 Jan 2018 12:56:23 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Changed dummy cache to &lt;tt&gt;Replicated&lt;/tt&gt; for now.&lt;br/&gt;
Merged to master: &lt;tt&gt;3dc1fcdaf1257a2a63c27dcb0e18d32495734cd3&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;
Cherry-picked to ignite-2.4: &lt;tt&gt;dd06d0bd7ef266bfbe156e858b312d1ac86e8982&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16330513" author="ptupitsyn" created="Thu, 18 Jan 2018 13:37:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Filed &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-7468&quot; title=&quot;Irrelevant &amp;quot;Caches have distinct sets of data nodes&amp;quot; error&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-7468&quot;&gt;IGNITE-7468&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
